    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">Given a string <var>s</var>, reverse it.<br><br>Then replace each mirrored character according to the following table:<br><br><pre style=\"font-family: monospace\">b &harr; d</pre>  <pre style=\"font-family: monospace\">p &harr; q</pre>   <pre style=\"font-family: monospace\">( &harr; )</pre>   <pre style=\"font-family: monospace\">[ &harr; ]</pre>   <pre style=\"font-family: monospace\">{ &harr; }</pre><br>All other characters remain unchanged.<br><br>Print the resulting string.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\">A single line containing the string <var>s</var>.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\">The transformed string.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\">1 &le; length of s &le; 30<br>s contains only printable ASCII characters.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">[pq]</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-out\">[pq]</pre>\n         </div>\n      </div>\n   </div>\n</div>"
